D1.summary:
Physics-first design starting from the operator form of the rendering equation and the K/C ownership contract. I defined ten properties a learned transport state must preserve: flux measure, non-negativity, linearity, passivity of iterated factors, reciprocity where applicable, rigid equivariance, explicit visibility, single path ownership, identifiability and independent validation. Each WL97 measure or energy failure is a violation of one of them:
- solid-angle-mean over-emission: measure mismatch;
- in-bin redistribution: a sub-cell lobe stored in a cell;
- emission-anchor and patch-spatial readout errors: position measure;
- non-passive learned local factors: a learned local operator where ER is exact;
- latent unsupervised sender: an unidentified intermediate.

Two further ECRO v0 violations are visible in the code and are not in WL97 [CODE model86.py:95,99]. The generator takes world centre, normal and tangent as inputs, plus a scene-global mean token. So ECRO's local factors are neither rigid-invariant nor dependency-local.

**Proposition I [PRED].** In the GM1 surface regime (planar/convex objects, pointwise frozen ER, point lights, explicit visibility), K equals ER exactly. Every transport quantity is then a deterministic functional of ER, geometry/visibility and emission. Learning can only do three things:
- (a) estimate integrals from fewer explicit queries;
- (b) amortize repeated application, which has a measured ceiling for the resolvent-only role on CK2;
- (c) infer what was not queried, which for free-space delivery means visibility.

**Carrier.** A flux-exact projected-disk (Nusselt) carrier: projected solid angle equals disk area. Sharp outgoing radiance is never tabulated; it is evaluated by ER at the exact direction from the stored incident state.

**Candidates.**
- A rejected: as a local kernel it is BRDF compression; as a nonlocal kernel it is learned C without a by-construction measure.
- B kept only as the carrier.
- C rejected on the sender side (ER compression), kept on the delivery side as the alternative.
- PRIMARY, XQT: a learned, linear, column-stochastic, visibility-masked redistribution of exact per-ray flux quanta. It is the flight operator at every order and is passive and flux-exact by construction.
- ALTERNATIVE, LLT: learned lobe form factor plus footprint density from sparse explicit probes. It is a different information regime and is gated by an information test.

**Flatland scratch (design input only).** Flux-conserving pooling of exact samples gains 8–50x in ray-equivalent terms over the unpooled gather. Almost all of that gain is available to the learning-free fixed-kernel twin: an exact-field oracle kernel beats the twin by only 1.0–1.33x in error (isotropic family only).

**Falsification plan.** Five stages, S0 to S5. Stage 1 is learning-free and can stop each candidate before training:
- H2 representation floors;
- the explicit quality–cost frontier;
- XQT oracle and twin ceilings;
- the LLT information test;
- H3 Amdahl and quality-matched ceilings.

S2 is the H1 arm (ECRO-COV with the same representation, corrected coverage and physical, non-M64 sender supervision). S3 trains the surviving candidates and S4 evaluates them on held-out workloads with fixed weights. S5 is quality-matched economics. CK2 stays diagnostic-only, with a new T1 reference.

**Verdict.** DESIGN_READY_FOR_HUMAN_REVIEW, conditional on HD-1, with the explicit prediction that a positive H3 result at the current scale is unlikely.

D2.verdict_rationale:
The design contains:
- one primary candidate (LIEM-S) with a complete contract;
- one representation-level alternative (LIEM-B);
- complete contracts and explicit rejection reasons for every other candidate (ECRO-lineage A/B/C, rigid-cluster self-transport, learned sharp delivery);
- a staged falsification plan that puts learning-free kill gates first (G0 ceilings, I0 headroom, I1 capacity) and only then training;
- arms separating H1 / H2 / H3 that share data, budget and reference where possible, with the non-shareable comparisons listed;
- every numerical threshold left to the human.

Not NO_DEFENSIBLE_CANDIDATE: LIEM-S satisfies P1-P8 and the brief's suitability criteria within its scope (learned rigid-reusable transport, no implicit visibility coupling, an energy contract by construction, independent reference validation planned), and its value over three named twins is measurable.

Not INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE: the decisive unknowns are measured cheaply inside the plan before any training. They are the cost-vs-sharpness headroom tension shown by the toy slab, refractive-media reference qualification, and representation capacity.

The verdict is conditional on HD2 / HD3 / HD7. For the GM1 surface-only scene86 family alone, D2's reading is that no defensible learned candidate exists. That reading is a design argument until G0 measures it.

This verdict is not adoption and not experiment approval.
